.TH MHVTL-CONTROL 8 "2026-10-28" "mhvtl-control 0.5.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mhvtl-control \- management daemon and web dashboard for the mhVTL virtual tape library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mhvtl-control
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mhvtl-control
serves a REST API under
.I /api/v1
and a web dashboard at
.IR / .
It reads the libraries and drives of a running mhVTL from
.IR device.conf ,
reads live library state and moves cartridges through each library's SCSI
medium changer, sends library commands over the mhVTL message queue, runs
.BR mktape (1)
and
.BR edit_tape (1)
to create and edit media, and runs
.B mhvtl-raw-format
to format raw disks as cartridges.
.PP
For monitoring,
.I /metrics
serves library, media, home filesystem and drive metrics in the Prometheus
text format,
.I /readyz
answers 200 when device.conf parses, every changer answers and every attached
raw-disk cartridge is readable (503 otherwise, with the failed checks), and
.I /healthz
answers 200 while the daemon runs.
.PP
.I /api/v1/service
reports the state of mhvtl.target, its support units and each
.B vtllibrary@
and
.B vtltape@
unit, the backend mhvtl.conf configures next to the modules loaded, and
whether the message queue exists. The unit states come from
.BR mhvtl-control-apply ;
without it,
.B manager
is
.B unavailable
and they are left out.
.PP
mhVTL may start after
.BR mhvtl-control ,
and may restart while it runs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-listen " addr"
Address to listen on. Default: 127.0.0.1:8080.
.B mhvtl-control
refuses a non-loopback address without a token, unless given
.BR \-insecure .
.IP
On loopback without a token, requests must name the daemon as localhost or a
loopback IP in Host, or get 421 Misdirected Request; this stops DNS rebinding. Behind a reverse proxy that passes the original
Host, set a token or have the proxy send Host: localhost.
.TP
.BI \-api\-token " token"
Bearer token required on
.IR /api/v1/* ,
.I /metrics
and
.IR /readyz .
Defaults to the
.B MHVTL_CONTROL_API_TOKEN
environment variable.
.TP
.B \-insecure
Allow a non-loopback
.B \-listen
address without a token.
.TP
.BI \-tls\-cert " file" " \-tls\-key " file
Serve HTTPS with this certificate and key.
.TP
.BI \-cors\-origin " origin"
Send Access-Control-Allow-Origin with this value. Default: CORS disabled.
.IP
POST, PATCH and DELETE requests a browser sends from any other origin (by
Sec-Fetch-Site or Origin) get 403; requests without those headers, as curl
sends them, are unaffected.
.B *
lets every origin through only when a token is set.
.TP
.BI \-config\-dir " dir"
Directory holding device.conf and library_contents.<id>. Default: /etc/mhvtl.
.TP
.BI \-home\-dir " dir"
Media home of a library for which neither device.conf nor mhvtl.conf gives
one. Default: /var/lib/mhvtl.
.TP
.BI \-changer " libid" = /dev/sgN
Use this node for a library's changer instead of finding it in sysfs.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-drive " driveid" = /dev/sgN
Use this node, or a link to it, for a drive instead of finding it in sysfs.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-mktape " path" ", \-edit\-tape " path ", \-format\-tool " path
Paths of mhVTL's mktape, edit_tape and mhvtl-raw-format. Default: found in
.BR PATH .
.TP
.BI \-vtltape " path"
Path of mhVTL's vtltape. Default: found in
.BR PATH ,
then in /usr/libexec/mhvtl and /usr/local/libexec/mhvtl, where mhVTL
installs its daemons. It is read, not run, to tell whether it has AES-GCM drive encryption; the
dashboard shows the drives of one older than markh794/mhvtl#328 as
simulated, and as unknown when it cannot be read.
.TP
.B \-include\-virtual
List loop, ram, dm and zram block devices among the disks.
.TP
.BI \-scan\-path " path"
Also inspect this disk or image path. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION EDITOR
The routes under
.I /api/v1/config
show and check device.conf, library_contents.<id> and mhvtl.conf. With
writes turned on they also change them: edits are staged in memory, checked
by a dry run of
.B POST /api/v1/config/apply
(with
.BR dry_run ),
then applied.
.B mhvtl-control
does not write the files itself:
.BR mhvtl-control-apply ,
started per request by
.BR mhvtl-control-apply.socket ,
writes them as root and restarts the affected
.B vtllibrary@
and
.B vtltape@
units. It accepts requests only from root processes of
.BR mhvtl-control.service .
.PP
Writes are off by default. They need an API token, TLS on a non-loopback
.BR \-listen ,
and the helper's socket:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl enable \-\-now mhvtl\-control\-apply.socket
systemctl enable mhvtl\-control\-apply\-recover.service
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B GET /api/v1/config/capabilities
reports
.B writes
as the first that holds of
.B helper_absent
(no helper socket),
.B tls_required
(non-loopback listen without TLS),
.B token_required
(no token),
.B helper_blocked
(/etc/mhvtl/mhvtl-control.env still exists, or an interrupted apply left an
unreadable intent), else
.BR ok .
.PP
During an apply, each affected library is offline to hosts. A cartridge in a
drive the apply stops makes the dry run answer
.B drive_loaded
with a force token, valid 120 seconds, with which the apply puts the
cartridge back in its slot. A failed apply is rolled back. An apply
interrupted by a crash is recovered by the next request, or at boot by
.BR mhvtl-control-apply-recover.service ,
which runs before mhVTL's units.
.PP
To turn writes off, first check that
.B helper
in the capabilities is neither
.B incomplete_apply
nor
.BR intent_unreadable ,
then disable both units again.
.SH SERVICE CONTROL
With writes on,
.B POST /api/v1/service/libraries/\fIid\fB/\fIaction\fR
starts, stops or restarts one library's
.B vtllibrary@
and
.B vtltape@
units, and
.B POST /api/v1/service/\fIaction\fR
mhvtl.target with every library and the support units;
.I action
is
.BR restart ,
.B stop
or
.BR start .
A dry run
.RB ( dry_run )
lists the units; the action takes them back in
.B units
and is refused (409
.BR unit )
if they changed. As for an apply, a loaded drive answers
.B drive_loaded
with a force token, a failed action is rolled back, and an interrupted one is
recovered. With PERSIST off, a library's placement is written to
library_contents.<id> before it stops. Starting a running library is refused
with
.BR use_restart ;
an action that with its rollback may not fit the helper's 30-minute
RuntimeMaxSec= with
.BR budget .
A stopped library stays down until started, and starts again at boot.
Moves and queue commands for the libraries an action affects wait until it
ends; an action waits at most a minute for a library one of them holds,
then answers 503
.BR busy .
.SH NOTES
Under
.BR mhvtl-control.service ,
media homes under /home, /root and /run/user are hidden from
.BR mhvtl-control ,
so mktape and edit_tape cannot reach them.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mhvtl-control/mhvtl-control.env
Options for
.BR mhvtl-control.service :
.B MHVTL_CONTROL_OPTS
and
.BR MHVTL_CONTROL_API_TOKEN .
.TP
.I /etc/mhvtl/mhvtl-control.env
Where 0.2.0 kept the options. Deprecated: while
.I /etc/mhvtl-control/mhvtl-control.env
is absent and neither variable is set,
.B mhvtl-control
reads this file itself and logs a warning.
.TP
.I /etc/mhvtl/device.conf
mhVTL's library and drive configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/mhvtl-control-apply
The configuration helper's state: intent.json for an apply under way,
rollback/ with the files each apply replaced, and the audit log audit.jsonl.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vtllibrary (1),
.BR vtltape (1),
.BR vtlcmd (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR mktape (1),
.BR edit_tape (1)
.PP
https://github.com/ciroiriarte/mhvtl-control
